==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fa|ستان|ـستان|tr=-estān}}, from {{der|en|pal|-stʾn'|tr=-estān}}, from {{der|en|peo|𐎿𐎫𐎠𐎴|ts=stāna}}, from {{der|en|ira-pro|*stā́nam}}, from {{der|en|iir-pro|*sthā́nam}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*steh₂-||to stand}}.

Compare {{cog|ae|𐬯𐬙𐬁𐬥𐬀}}, {{cog|sa|स्थान|tr=sthā́na}}, {{cog|ru|стан}} (< {{cog|sla-pro|*stanъ}}), {{cog|en|stay}}, {{m|en|stand}}, {{m|en|state}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|en|suffix}}

# [[home]] of; [[place]] where one [[stay]]s; used especially in place names

====Usage notes====
Corresponding [[demonym]] usually formed by suffixing {{m|en|-i}}, yielding {{m|en||-stani}}. When the root is an ethnicity, the {{m|en||-stani}} form refers to the nationality, not ethnicity. Compare {{m|en|Tajik||member of Tajik ethnic group}} and {{m|en|Tajikistani||inhabitant of nation of Tajikistan}}.

